# Accepted-risk suppressions for the Trivy security scan (CI).
#
# All remaining findings below affect `next` 14.2.35 (frontend) and are only
# fixed in Next.js 15.5+/16.x. Upgrading is a major framework migration
# (React 19 / App Router breaking changes) tracked separately; it cannot be
# done as part of a CI fix. Risk notes:
# - The frontend has no middleware.ts, is not exposed directly (nginx fronts
#   it) and this is a simulated-trading platform with no real funds.
# - The findings are DoS/SSRF/info-disclosure in Server Components and
#   middleware paths we do not use.
# Review when the Next.js 15 migration lands.

# Information disclosure due to middleware bypass (no middleware in this app)
CVE-2026-44573
# SSRF via crafted requests (fix only in 15.5.16/16.2.5)
CVE-2026-44578
# DoS via crafted requests to App Router (fix only in 15.5.21/16.2.11)
CVE-2026-64641
# SSRF vulnerability (fix only in 15.x/16.x)
CVE-2026-64645
# SSRF via malicious requests (fix only in 15.x/16.x)
CVE-2026-64649
# DoS with Server Components (fix only in 15.5.16/16.2.5)
GHSA-8h8q-6873-q5fj
# HTTP request deserialization DoS (fix only in 15.x)
GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf
# DoS with Server Components (fix only in 15.5.15/16.2.3)
